'''Healingcraft''' is a branch of [[Magic|magic]] that deals in healing the human body. It is considered [[Forbidden Magic]] to [[Pointed Cap Witches]] and has been lost since the [[Day of the Pact]].{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}}

== Description ==
Those that practiced Healingcraft are known as Witches of Healingcraft, or simply Healers. They held an understanding of medicine, apothecary and the human body, and sought to use their magic to help others by healing the sick, weak and injured. Due to Pact stipulating that magic should not be cast on the body, Healingcraft inherently violates the principles set out on the Day of the Pact.{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}}

=== Healingcraft Magic ===
'''Potions and Essential Tonics'''

Concoctions of a medicinal and magical variety. Not much is known about them, apart from there being several different kinds, each brewed for the purpose of curing and healing others. They were also shared amongst healers through the [[Twinned Bottles]] [[contraption]].{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}}

'''Twinned Bottles'''
: ''See also: [[Twinned Bottles]]''
An ancient contraption of medicine in which a small medallion etched with a [[Spells|Casting Seal]] would be placed inside two bottles. The spell allowed for the contents of the two vessels to remain evenly split, no matter the distance between them.{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}}

'''Immortality and Necromancy'''

Some witches sought to attain eternal life or raise the dead, and resorted to human experimentation in order to achieve this. Whether or not they succeeded remains unclear.{{Ref|m|30|19-20}}{{Ref|m|20|2}}
