== History ==
[[File:Anime S1E09 Healingcraft Witches Resist Pact.png|240px|thumb|<small>The Righteous Witches of Healingcraft resist the Wise Ones' Pact</small>]]
The Witches of Healingcraft were highly prevalent in the events leading up to the Day of the Pact. They were the last to resist the [[Three Wise|Wise Ones’]] edict that magic should not be cast upon the body.{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}} Despite their noble intentions, their goals and methodology were deemed far too dangerous to allow — especially that of those who resorted to vile experimentation on human subjects, actions that would ultimately lead to war.{{Ref|m|30|19-20}} Thus, when the memory of magic was wiped from the populace, so too were the feats of Healingcraft and the witches that practiced it lost to history.{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}}

What remains of Healingcraft magic now primarily belongs to that of the [[Brimmed Caps]], though its influence and legacy still prevail to this day.{{Ref|a|9}}{{Ref|m|15|2-3}} The history of Healingcraft is a fundamental lesson taught to schoolchildren studying to become [[Witches|witches]]. Pointed Cap Witches are forbidden from studying medicine as a result of what happened among the witches practicing Healingcraft long ago. Additionally, those aiming to become [[Doctor|doctors]] must never learn magic, making it a profession restricted only to [[Outsiders|outsiders]].{{Ref|m|30|19-20}} This stipulation of the Pact is known to doctors as well, even if they may not know the origins behind this code.{{Ref|m|17|16-17}}{{Ref|m|59|9-11}}

Witches of Healingcraft have been shown to wear a crest that bears similarity to the one doctors wear in the present. Doctors can be viewed as the successors to ancient healers, now that the domain of medicine falls to their shoulders. The King of Life, [[Deanreldy]] of [[Ezrest]] is the last direct descendant of an ancient and proud house known for its skill with Healingcraft.{{Ref|m|53|23}}
